    "created_at": "2021-08-16T09:34:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-08-16T10:24:08Z",
    "body": "There must be more to this.\r\n\r\nDemo: https://github.com/jakearchibald/send-more-bytes-than-length\r\n\r\nThis sets up an HTTP/1.1 endpoint that sets a `Content-Length` of 1000 but sends 1500 bytes.\r\n\r\nChrome, Firefox, and Safari all successfully receive the response truncated to 1000 bytes. The server definitely sends all 1500 bytes.\r\n\r\nMaybe things are different with combinations of chunked encoding / HTTP/2, + range requests + content encoding?",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
