    "created_at": "2021-08-16T10:12:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-08-16T10:12:23Z",
    "body": "I should add, it's possible to check if there are any bytes currently pending on a socket, and read them if there are, and don't do anything if there aren't, but that's not an operation any browser's TCP logic has previously had to support.  Chrome does have that ability in its socket layer now (with SSL support that doesn't get confused by extra SSL control messages, I believe), but didn't for most of its existence.\r\n\r\nAs previously noted, of course, that effort is necessarily best-effort, and could get confused by other messages over the wire.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
